  "entry": "code/src/spatialaim/gui/app.py",
  "notes": "Found in a public repository and run by a computer-use agent (batch public-1). Load a raw-count scRNA reference and a spatial transcriptomics slice, over-cluster and agglomerate the reference, map spots to cell states with one or more mappers across every K, and pick the cell-state granularity that maps most reliably, judged by reconstruction, spatial organisation and transcriptional coherence. Data used in the run: example. tree.json is the workflow the agent did and a second agent replayed; run.json says how.",
